AccountV3 user-controlled UUPS
├── Given the standard UUPS selector, an implementation, a proxy, a caller or EntryPoint
│   └── It cannot bypass typed proposal and commit authority
├── Given an active account and a proposed UpgradeManifest
│   ├── It binds account, chain, predecessor, version, nonce, target code and layout
│   ├── It requires distinct current ADMIN votes; spend/purpose replay never suffices
│   ├── It rejects another pending proposal and validity shorter than the wait
│   └── Its minimum 72h wait starts at acceptance, not a backdated signature
├── Given a queued upgrade
│   ├── Current ADMIN quorum can cancel; expiry never restores consumed nonces
│   ├── Freeze cancels a pending upgrade irreversibly
│   └── It needs a fresh CommitProposal, acknowledgements and current admin quorum
├── Given target compatibility metadata
│   ├── Wrong UUPS/layout/EntryPoint, code drift, missing or malformed responses fail
│   ├── Every invalid target category runs deterministically and preserves the previous state
│   └── Gas and returndata bombs fail within a bounded metadata read
└── Given a valid mature commit
    ├── It preserves identity, policy, funds and nonces; increments securityVersion
    ├── Old signatures fail; new direct and EntryPoint operations still work
    ├── Only the exact migration bytes run; reverting/corrupting migrations roll back
    ├── Every core corruption and explicit migration revert runs deterministically with its exact error
    ├── Spend callbacks cannot use even otherwise-valid admin consent
    └── Fixed library drift fails closed; metadata does not replace bytecode review
